Beat `when:` narrowing of a <match> subject (cheatsheet "Match & when": "A beat's when: narrows the subject for the whole body").
lute check-project .   (s.lute is written with the last variant)
  when: run.accused != 'none'                          -> ok (narrowed: none not required)
  when: run.accused == 'tilly'                         -> E-ARM-DEAD on hester/ruben arms (narrowed)
  when: run.accused == 'tilly' || run.accused == 'hester'  -> E-NONEXHAUSTIVE `none` not covered; `ruben` arm NOT flagged dead
  when: run.accused in ['tilly', 'hester']            -> same as the || form
Expected: the disjunction / `in` list narrows to {tilly, hester} like the single == does, so the match needs
no dead `<otherwise>` and the `ruben` arm is reported E-ARM-DEAD.
